  "description": "Direct entry of binary instruction patterns into computer memory via front-panel switches or hex keyboards. Before assemblers or compilers exist, this is the only way to make a computer execute programs. The bootstrap loader — a tiny program toggled in by hand that loads larger programs from storage — is the bridge from tedious manual entry to automated program loading.",
